222|                    // Set bits to the number of bits not yet consumed from the
223|                    // last byte. If we are at the end of the block, bits is
224|                    // either the number of bits in the last byte belonging to
225|                    // the next block, or the number of pad bits after the
226|                    // final block. In either of those cases, bits is in the
227|                    // range 0..7.
